  "worked_solution": "If the remaining distance to the destination is $D$ meters, then the rate of the change of distance is $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in minutes.\n\nSince the cyclist is $200$ meters closer each minute, the rate of change of remaining distance is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-200.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the remaining distance is *decreasing*.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
